From: grimtickle-overlay (local)
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cix: fix uninitialised 'status' in dailink status check

cix_dailink_status_check() declared `const char *status;` uninitialised and
then dereferenced it whenever of_property_read_string() failed to set it
(the "status" property is absent), which is undefined behaviour. Initialise
it to NULL so an absent property is well-defined and treated as "okay".
The `ret` variable was assigned but never used; drop it.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c b/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c
index 15080dd..49958ff 100644
--- a/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c
+++ b/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c
@@ -108,10 +108,9 @@ static int cix_dailink_parsing_fmt(struct device_node *np,
 /* only disabled dai-link status, not continue to parse */
 static bool cix_dailink_status_check(struct device_node *np)
 {
-	const char *status;
-	int ret;
+	const char *status = NULL;
 
-	ret = of_property_read_string(np, "status", &status);
+	of_property_read_string(np, "status", &status);
 
 	if (status) {
 		if (!strcmp(status, "okay") || !strcmp(status, "ok"))
